; ClickHouse endpoint for the cron-job metrics hooks (src/utils/clickhouse.php).
;
; Sections are keyed by the `clickhouse:<name>` tag (the same tag hlab's
; clickhouse/srv/<name>-D0<GUID>/default.toml declares as its `db`); this
; client reads [clickhouse:analytics], the database the simox_job_runs /
; simox_job_counters schema lives in.
;
; Endpoint-only: host and port of the HTTPS interface. The SQL user is the
; global CLICKHOUSE_USER (default `default`); the password stays empty by
; policy — mutual TLS with the machine client certificate (SSL_DIR) is the
; security boundary, so no credential is shipped here.
;
; hlab's `doric` CLI uses the native-protocol port on the same server; this
; client speaks the HTTPS interface, which is what a PHP process can reach
; without a native driver.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only and is MANUALLY MAINTAINED by the
; consumer (private data: copied into etc/ as a real file by simox's
; bin/fetch-private-data in dev, shipped into the freshly swapped etc/ by the
; framework's DEPLOY_PRIVATE_FILES — see doc/system/private-config.md). The
; committed copy is this template: placeholders only, never a real endpoint.
; An absent etc/clickhouse.ini disables metrics; it never fails a job.

[clickhouse:analytics]
host = 10.99.x.x
port = 8443
